# Snapshots are CAPTURES, not source.
#
# Each one is a record of what one side answered at one instant against a live,
# mutable, single-homed corpus. Committing them would imply they are a baseline
# you can diff against later — they are not: the corpus moves, so a snapshot is
# only meaningful against its counterpart taken minutes earlier. The frozen
# artefact in this harness is queries.json, not the answers.
#
# They also contain the ids of one person's private memories.
#
# Keep the directory, ignore the contents.
*.json
